# The D3D11 reference for sky-river-org1.env: the engine draws the sky (CS_ORG_SKY unset), Cloud Shadows' copy on the graph in
# both. Riverwood's river by the mill in cloudy weather (12f2d) at 13:00 and 22:00: a shot down at the river (the water's
# reflection of the sky and its clouds, from the reflection faces) and one up at the sky each time, then Dragonsreach.
CS_ORG_CLOUD_SHADOWS=1
DXVK_DEBUG=hang
VK_LOADER_LAYERS_DISABLE=*nsight*
CS_DCLF_TEST_COMMANDS=600:set timescale to 0;601:set gamehour to 13;602:fw 12f2d;700:coc Riverwood;1800:set timescale to 20;1810:fw 12f2d;1880:set timescale to 0;1881:set gamehour to 13;1900:player.setpos x 19300;1901:player.setpos y -45300;1902:player.setpos z -80;1910:player.setangle x 12;1911:player.setangle z 0;2300:dclf:shot=river-noon;2310:player.setangle x -60;2600:dclf:shot=river-sky-noon;2610:player.setangle x 12;2620:set timescale to 20;2621:set gamehour to 22;2630:fw 12f2d;2700:set timescale to 0;2701:set gamehour to 22;3000:dclf:shot=river-night;3010:player.setangle x -60;3300:dclf:shot=river-sky-night;3310:coc WhiterunDragonsreach;4300:dclf:shot=dragonsreach
CS_DCLF_TEST_EXIT=4400
